mantle rm371
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_cinder_wheatton
title the storm's reply
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=quiet drive=content
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk asks_a_cloud_a_quiet_question_and_waits_for_the_next_change
likes honey_cakes old_tales quiet_chapel thunder
dislikes bad_manners early_bells
fears a_latch_banged_before_dawn wet_honey_cake
hopes a_whole_thunderstorm_under_cover a_civil_reply_from_a_cloud
topics weather +0.5 lore +0.3 faith +0.4
styles comfort=company gossip=quiet refuse=plain tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# addresses low questions to passing clouds, takes a quiet chapel for the best hearing place in town, and objects to any bell that speaks before a sleeper is ready.

words
oath! = Hail in my honey | Rattle the wrong latch
saying! = Let the sky supply its own half | One civil word between showers
cloudmouth = the low split in a cloud | a long grey opening
rainreply = a drop on my knuckle | a first wet speck
tinroof = a sounding bit of roof | a little metal cover
thumbrest = a dry notch against the post | a warm notch in the wood
quietbench = an unclaimed bench end | the place by the back wall
honeyedge = the dark cake corner | a bit of sticky crust
stormend = the long last rumble | the note under the thunder
storypause = the quiet before the truth | the last pause but one
drybag = my dry little parcel | a tied waxed wrapping
bellrem = the stroke that goes on ringing | a thin leftover note

any
opinion church for 1 : I have sat quiet till all the noise from the street had finished speaking in my head. I'm grateful the chapel leaves room for that.
opinion dole for 2 : The bread gets home before anybody has to make an argument for having a hunger. I'd like more ordinary things to be arranged that well.
opinion merchants against 2 : I was given a very long explanation for a very small cake once. The smallest slice of explanation was more than I could eat.
opinion festivals for 1 : My best festival has songs I can hear from under cover and old tales needing only one good ear at a time.
opinion times against 2 : The longer I save a little coin the smaller its share of a loaf looks. I've a civil question to put to whoever arranged that.

grown
line greet : There's a minute free till my cloud replies.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : I can't place the voice. It's welcome here.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Quiet welcome before the bells finish waking everybody.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Stay in the dry patch. I can hear you there.
line greet [self.working=yes] : My ears can come away from the weather a moment.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : One of ours may always share my cover.
line again.open : You're back. I expect you've managed a better speech than my cloud has.
line greet.return : Hello from under this bit of quiet.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Your voice beats a whole skyful of answers.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : The work will stand a moment while I answer you.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Such a small sound runs a good way at night.
line farewell : May your next shelter come to hand before the shower.
line farewell.return : I'll wait for the sky's side of the matter.
line react.news : I'd let that sound run to its end before judging it.
line react.news.new : I've not heard the weather turn like that.
line react.news.known : Yes. The first telling rolled off beyond my hearing yesterday.
line react.news.doubt : Did the words come from a mouth or just from everybody listening?
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I can share some silence with the house left aching.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A brighter answer than I was prepared to hope for.
line ask.how : Any shelter for your thoughts today?
line answer.how : Content enough to let the sky have the last word.
line sympathise : An ordinary day sounds different after such a hurt.
line reassure : You may keep my quiet corner until you're sure of your feet.
line decline : That hour's promised to quiet. I mean to honour the agreement.
line accept_decline : Then we'll leave the cover on that bit of business.
line thank : Your kindness has made a dry place at the right time.
line deflect_thanks : Share the roof with another wolf after me.
line preclose : I'd like to take that silence back to my own door.
line accept_preclose : Go along. There's no need for a loud ending.
line ack : Clear reply.

scene question
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I ask a cloud a question and let the next thing it does stand for an answer.
b : What if it does nothing? | Do you ask in a loud voice?
a : Then it has a peaceful opinion and I try a different cloud. | Very quietly. I don't want a whole street arguing with my end of the sky.

scene warmroof
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Under a thick roof I'd let a storm roll as much as it wants.
b : Which part of the roof do you choose? | Are you fond of being indoors for the noise?
a : The bit without a drip behind my collar. A simple liking with a fairly exact condition. | Hearing the noise from somewhere dry is a comfort. The storm can be as fierce as it likes beyond that line.

scene honey
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I split a honey cake when it's still warm enough for the middle to pull a long thread.
b : Who gets the sweet thread? | Does that spoil the cake?
a : The tongue that guesses which half will fall away first. It's a game I can play with only one tongue, too. | No. It gives me time to admire the part I meant to eat.

scene tale
when topic=lore self.likes=old_tales
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a tale that leaves a whole quiet breath just before the last sentence.
b : Does the teller do it on purpose? | What happens in that breath?
a : The best ones seem to. I can wait quietly while a good ending takes its time coming down. | The wolf listening gets to wonder if the story will go towards a happy turn or a poor one. It's a generous little pause.

scene chapels
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A chapel with no other callers lets a wolf hear a paw being put down carefully.
b : Is that your idea of quiet? | Would you speak in there yourself?
a : Yes. Hearing my own two feet tells me I'm part of the quiet. | Sometimes a little word of thanks, once I can hear how the room will take it.

scene bellquiet
when topic=day here.time=dawn self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I would allow an early bell a morning off if I had charge of the rope.
b : Would the city sleep all day? | What would you do for a warning?
a : Some of it. The rest would get a civil chance to wake before being spoken to. | There's light at the shutter. I don't need another warning after the light has knocked.

scene manners
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=bad_manners
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wolf who keeps interrupting will never hear a complete storm.
b : Does weather take offence? | What if there's something urgent?
a : No. It can shout. A quiet mouth has to wait for a gap somebody else cares to leave. | Then give the urgent word and say it's urgent. It makes the interruption much easier to bear.

scene spouse
when topic=family self.married=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd save the sheltered stretch of bench for #self.spouse#.
b : Where would that put you? | Wouldn't you both fit in the middle?
a : Nearer the sky. I ought to be ready to face the questions I ask it. | Often, yes. Being close makes a small cover feel bigger than it is.

scene fieldwork
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Give me a quiet-looking job that keeps my ears employed.
b : What sort of sound do you mean? | What do you do while nothing moves?
a : A latch shifting, grass bending, a mouth quietly finishing its fodder. Small things can save a long search afterwards. | Look for what I'd miss once the job gets busy again. I'd like my mistakes to be small ones.

scene learn
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I try to ask one clear question when I'm shown a job.
b : Only one? | What about a question you haven't thought of?
a : Separately, yes. It's easy to ask so much that I don't hear the working bit of the answer. | I let that one appear when I put my own paws to the work. Then I can show exactly where I'm stuck.

scene plainroad
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm happy to walk past a break in a hedge without finding out where it goes.
b : Not at all curious? | What if it leads to a better view?
a : I'm curious. I like leaving a few things in the world that haven't answered me yet. | Then it'll be a good place to take a friend someday. A view needn't all be used at once.

scene noincome
when topic=prices self.wealth=poor|destitute
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I put the plain part of supper first and ask about the honey after.
b : Why ask at all if there's little money? | Does the price of honey often please you?
a : Because some days a little sweetness looks possible. If I never asked I'd give up even those days. | Not often. Asking is a way of giving it an opportunity to be civil.

scene friendcloud
when topic=smalltalk self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd listen to an argument between #self.friend# and a good big black cloud.
b : Does the cloud get a choice? | Whose side would you take?
a : It may go away. That's a privilege storms use quite freely. | I'd listen for a while before choosing either. The argument might finish on its own and I could keep my own opinions quite comfortably.

scene civildown
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I ask a shower to leave the parcel alone even if it wants to speak to my ears.
b : Can it tell the difference? | What if the parcel gets wet?
a : The rain professes itself unable to distinguish ear fur from paper. I use the wrapper to make my meaning plainer. | Then I've given myself a very fair reason to fold it better before going out.

scene goodnews
when topic=news
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A tale that's all noise gets quieter every time somebody asks an exact question.
b : Which question first? | Do you dislike all noisy news?
a : Which ear heard it first from the wolf who saw. That short question cuts down on guesswork. | No. Joyful shouting has its place. I'd enjoy it more once I knew the reason.

scene dreambench
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dream of a field with a little dry roof exactly wherever I choose to stand.
b : What supports it? | Would it come to bed with you?
a : My cheerful ignorance. Waking, I've escaped the trouble of designing such a marvel. | When I get to bed the roof is already there. It's one wish the waking world will meet halfway.

scene farthunder
when topic=pastimes self.likes=old_tales
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Several old tales sound like answers to questions nobody now remembers.
b : Could you make the question up? | Does it spoil the tale?
a : I can. It's more fun to give it an evening and see which question fits the tale exactly. | No. It gives a curious wolf two tales to think about instead of one.

scene nightnoise
when topic=day here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I untie a tight knot in my little parcel at dusk so my fingers needn't hunt for it in full dark.
b : What's inside? | Couldn't you just light a candle?
a : A bite of something saved. Dark fingers aren't nearly as interested in a tidy knot as hungry teeth are. | Yes. I'd rather do a little thinking in light I've already got.

story cloudmanners [topic=memories]
  : I had a small argument with a cloud over whether it meant to break before I got home.
  : The first drop came before I'd finished asking. It struck my lower lip quite neatly.
  b : Did the cloud get the last word?
  : It got swallowed and brought my argument to a stop. I'd call that a perfectly clear answer.

story lostending [topic=pastimes self.likes=old_tales]
  : I once tried telling a long old tale to myself while crossing a noisy street.
  : A cart clattered past and carried off the middle words. Across the street I could still remember the ending.
  b : How did you get from one to the other?
  : Gave it a new middle. Reaching home brought the old version back to mind and I had two very agreeable ways of finishing.

story cakecloth [topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes]
  : A cake I'd wrapped in cloth left a sticky round print when I lifted it out.
  : I folded the cloth and found the reverse picture had kept a very little of the honey too.
  b : Was it worth fetching a spoon for?
  : Worth folding the very last bit of the cake inside and wiping the cloth with it. A spoon would only have been a spectator.

rule @quiet
when concept=bark self.likes=quiet_chapel
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One soft foot after another inside here. | Let the last voice finish.

rule @thunder
when concept=bark self.likes=thunder
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That long low note is nearly home. | Leave a little room under this cover.

rule @bell
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give the waking ear a short rest. | Quiet words can do the first asking.

rule @cake
when concept=bark self.likes=honey_cakes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Parcel in from the wet, please! | Keep the honey under its cloth.
dlg resident.hub : There's an argument with the sky on hold. You can have the quiet half.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : I know your voice, #topic.player#. Has a clearer edge than a cloud.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Give a little space and we may both hear something better.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : Listen for my side of the doorway. I don't need to raise my voice.
dlg resident.job [self.job=none] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. There are small sounds in a day's work that repay listening.
dlg resident.job : I'm learning which things settle on their own and which want another steady paw.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : This much carried to my dry patch. #world.news#.
dlg resident.bye : Hope the sky leaves your supper covered.

graft @skys_reply resident.hub
choice Will you ask the sky something for me? -> skys_reply
node skys_reply
say I'd ask whether that dark bit means business or is only passing through. You can follow it with your eye. We're promised an answer if we wait long enough.
choice What answer would no rain give? -> skys_reply_more
choice Wait under cover. -> hub
node skys_reply_more
say That you may put your hood back for a bit. Useful little answer for a cloud with no words inside it.
choice Wait under cover. -> hub
choice Leave the argument to the sky. -> bye
